1
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:05,980
A night the earth didn't sleep.

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:09,640
Strange things were happening in the countryside of northeast Hebei.

3
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:14,900
For three days the water in the village wells rose and fell,

4
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,140
rose and fell.

5
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:20,320
Farmers noticed that the well walls had deep cracks in them.

6
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,040
A smelly gas came out of the cracks.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,520
In the farmyards, the chickens and even the pigs were too nervous to eat.

8
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:32,100
Mice ran out of the fields looking for places to hide.

9
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,620
Fish jumped out of their bowls and ponds.

10
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:47,840
The sound of planes could be heard outside the city of Tangshan even

11
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,600
when no planes were in the sky.

12
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:54,300
In the city, the water pipes in some buildings cracked and burst.

13
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:57,100
But the one million people of the city,

14
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:59,060
who thought little of these events,

15
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,380
were asleep as usual that night.

16
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,340
It seemed as if the world was at an end!

17
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,820
One-third of the nation felt it.

18
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:36,080
Steam burst from holes in the ground.

19
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:39,520
Hard hills of rock became rivers of dirt.

20
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:48,560
The suffering of the people was extreme.

21
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:53,220
Two-thirds of them died or were injured during the earthquake.

22
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:57,760
Thousands of families were killed and many children were left

23
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,680
without parents.

24
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:05,160
The number of people who were killed or injured reached more than 400,000.

25
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,740
But how could the survivors believe it was natural?

26
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:25,800
Bricks covered the ground like red autumn leaves.

27
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:29,120
No wind, however, could blow them away.

28
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:39,560
The railway tracks were now useless pieces of steel.

29
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:44,120
Tens of thousands of cows would never give milk again.

30
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:48,120
Half a million pigs and millions of chickens were dead.

31
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,580
Sand now filled the wells instead of water.

32
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,540
People were shocked.

33
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:05,100
Some of the rescue workers and doctors were trapped under the ruins.

34
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,500
More buildings fell down.

35
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,600
Water, food, and electricity were hard to get.

36
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:15,220
People began to wonder how long the disaster would last.

37
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:17,700
All hope was not lost.

38
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,920
Hundreds of thousands of people were helped.

39
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:31,940
The army organized teams to dig out those who were trapped

40
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,100
and to bury the dead.

41
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,400
To the north of the city,

42
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:39,680
most of the10,000 miners were rescued from the coal mines there.

43
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:44,140
Workers built shelters for survivors whose homes had been destroyed.

44
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,740
Fresh water was taken to the city by train,

45
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,320
truck and plane.

46
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:52,640
Slowly, the city began to breathe again.
